GUIDES = {'how-to-choose-an-ai-image-tool': {'title': 'How to Choose an AI Image Tool: A Practical Decision Guide',
                                    'description': 'A practical framework for choosing between image '
                                                   'generators, editors, background removers and upscalers '
                                                   'without paying for the wrong workflow.',
                                    'updated': 'September 4, 2026',
                                    'intro': 'The phrase AI image tool covers several different products. A '
                                             'text-to-image generator, a product-photo editor and a '
                                             'background remover may all use AI, but they solve different '
                                             'problems. The fastest way to choose well is to start with the '
                                             'output you need, then evaluate control, editing, consistency '
                                             'and cost.',
                                    'sections': [{'heading': '1. Start with the job, not the brand',
                                                  'body': 'If you need a new image from an idea, start with '
                                                          'a generator such as ChatGPT, Midjourney, Firefly, '
                                                          'Canva AI or Leonardo. If the image already exists '
                                                          'and only needs cleanup, an editor such as Pixlr '
                                                          'or PhotoRoom may be faster. If the only problem '
                                                          'is the background, a focused tool such as '
                                                          'Remove.bg avoids unnecessary complexity. If the '
                                                          'image is too small, an upscaler is the relevant '
                                                          'category.'},
                                                 {'heading': '2. Decide how much control you really need',
                                                  'body': 'Beginners often benefit from conversational or '
                                                          'template-led workflows because they reduce setup '
                                                          'time. More advanced creators may care about '
                                                          'repeatable styles, references, model controls, '
                                                          'aspect ratios and asset organization. More '
                                                          'control is not automatically better: extra '
                                                          'settings can slow a one-off social graphic but '
                                                          'become valuable when a project contains dozens of '
                                                          'related assets.'},
                                                 {'heading': '3. Separate artistic quality from production '
                                                             'usefulness',
                                                  'body': 'An image can look impressive and still be '
                                                          'inconvenient in a production workflow. Marketing '
                                                          'teams may care about editable layouts, brand '
                                                          'assets and text placement. Concept artists may '
                                                          'care more about mood, composition and style. '
                                                          'E-commerce sellers may value clean product '
                                                          'cutouts and consistent backgrounds above artistic '
                                                          'expression.'},
                                                 {'heading': '4. Check consistency and iteration costs',
                                                  'body': 'AI generation usually requires iteration. A tool '
                                                          'that produces attractive first results can still '
                                                          'become expensive if every usable asset needs many '
                                                          'reruns. Consider how easily you can refine an '
                                                          'existing result, preserve a subject, reuse a '
                                                          'reference and keep a visual direction across '
                                                          'multiple outputs.'},
                                                 {'heading': '5. A two-tool workflow can be better than one',
                                                  'body': 'One product does not need to solve every stage. A '
                                                          'creator might generate concept art in Midjourney, '
                                                          'refine an alternate in ChatGPT, remove a '
                                                          'background with Remove.bg and assemble the '
                                                          'campaign in Canva. Specialized tools can be more '
                                                          'efficient than forcing one platform to perform '
                                                          'tasks outside its strengths.'}],
                                    'takeaways': ['Choose the tool category before choosing the brand.',
                                                  'Match control level to the complexity of the project.',
                                                  'Evaluate the complete workflow, not only the first '
                                                  'generated image.',
                                                  'Factor iteration and credit limits into real cost.',
                                                  'Combining specialized tools can be more efficient than '
                                                  'using one platform for everything.']},
 'chatgpt-vs-midjourney-vs-firefly': {'title': 'ChatGPT vs Midjourney vs Adobe Firefly: Which Image Workflow '
                                               'Fits You?',
                                      'description': 'A workflow-focused comparison of conversational '
                                                     'iteration, art-direction-first generation and '
                                                     'Adobe-oriented production.',
                                      'updated': 'September 4, 2026',
                                      'intro': 'ChatGPT, Midjourney and Adobe Firefly can all generate '
                                               'images, but their workflows are different enough that asking '
                                               'which one is simply best is not very useful. A better '
                                               'question is whether you want conversational iteration, '
                                               'art-direction-focused generation or integration with a '
                                               'professional design ecosystem.',
                                      'sections': [{'heading': 'ChatGPT: when the brief is still evolving',
                                                    'body': 'ChatGPT is useful when image creation is part '
                                                            'of a conversation. You can discuss the idea, '
                                                            'ask for alternatives, change individual '
                                                            'elements and refine the brief without treating '
                                                            'every attempt as an isolated prompt. This is '
                                                            'practical for marketers, general creators and '
                                                            'users who prefer natural-language iteration.'},
                                                   {'heading': 'Midjourney: when visual style is the '
                                                               'objective',
                                                    'body': 'Midjourney is strongly associated with art '
                                                            'direction, mood and expressive concept '
                                                            'generation. It suits users who enjoy exploring '
                                                            'variations and developing a visual direction '
                                                            'through prompting. It can be less convenient '
                                                            'when the final deliverable depends on exact '
                                                            'typography, rigid layout or a broader '
                                                            'business-design workflow.'},
                                                   {'heading': 'Firefly: when generation belongs inside '
                                                               'design production',
                                                    'body': 'Firefly becomes more attractive when the output '
                                                            'will continue into Adobe creative work. '
                                                            'Generative editing, image creation and '
                                                            'production tools can sit closer together for '
                                                            'designers already using the Adobe ecosystem. '
                                                            'The workflow advantage can matter more than '
                                                            'comparing isolated showcase images.'},
                                                   {'heading': 'The practical decision',
                                                    'body': 'Choose ChatGPT for conversational refinement, '
                                                            'Midjourney for visual exploration and Firefly '
                                                            'for an Adobe-centered production workflow. For '
                                                            'some professionals, more than one tool makes '
                                                            'sense because ideation and final production '
                                                            'have different requirements.'}],
                                      'takeaways': ['ChatGPT emphasizes conversational iteration.',
                                                    'Midjourney emphasizes visual style and concept '
                                                    'exploration.',
                                                    'Firefly emphasizes integration with Adobe-oriented '
                                                    'production.',
                                                    'The final workflow matters more than a single showcase '
                                                    'image.']},
 'runway-vs-pika-vs-luma': {'title': 'Runway vs Pika vs Luma: Choosing an AI Video Generator by Workflow',
                            'description': 'Compare three generative-video workflows for production-oriented '
                                           'creation, fast short clips and cinematic motion experiments.',
                            'updated': 'September 4, 2026',
                            'intro': 'Runway, Pika and Luma can all create AI video, but they are useful for '
                                     'different creator profiles. The main differences are workflow depth, '
                                     'speed of experimentation and how much production control you expect '
                                     'around the generated clip.',
                            'sections': [{'heading': 'Runway: broader creative production',
                                          'body': 'Runway is a better fit for users who want multiple '
                                                  'generative and transformation tools in one creative '
                                                  'environment. It rewards creators who are willing to learn '
                                                  'a broader toolkit and iterate on references, prompts and '
                                                  'edits. That makes it attractive for filmmakers and visual '
                                                  'creators, but potentially more than a casual user needs '
                                                  'for one short effect.'},
                                         {'heading': 'Pika: fast short-form experimentation',
                                          'body': 'Pika is well suited to quickly turning an image or idea '
                                                  'into a short moving visual. The lower conceptual barrier '
                                                  'makes it useful for social creators testing hooks, motion '
                                                  'effects or playful concepts. Its strength is rapid '
                                                  'experimentation rather than long-form continuity.'},
                                         {'heading': 'Luma: visually ambitious motion concepts',
                                          'body': 'Luma is attractive when the goal is cinematic motion, '
                                                  'atmosphere or an ambitious concept shot. Like other '
                                                  'generative-video tools, it may require several attempts '
                                                  'to align subject, camera and motion. It is best '
                                                  'approached as a creative generation engine rather than '
                                                  'deterministic animation software.'},
                                         {'heading': 'The practical choice',
                                          'body': 'Pick Runway for a broader production-oriented AI '
                                                  'workspace, Pika for fast short clips and image animation, '
                                                  'and Luma for motion-focused cinematic exploration. '
                                                  'Whichever you choose, budget time for iteration and use a '
                                                  'conventional editor for final audio, captions and '
                                                  'assembly.'}],
                            'takeaways': ['Runway offers the broadest production-style workflow of the '
                                          'three.',
                                          'Pika is well matched to fast short-form experiments.',
                                          'Luma is a strong option for cinematic motion exploration.',
                                          'None replaces a full editor for final assembly, audio and '
                                          'captions.']},
 'ai-video-workflow-for-shorts': {'title': 'A Practical AI Video Workflow for TikTok, Reels and YouTube '
                                           'Shorts',
                                  'description': 'A step-by-step workflow for combining AI generation with '
                                                 'editing, captions and retention-focused short-form '
                                                 'production.',
                                  'updated': 'September 4, 2026',
                                  'intro': 'Short-form video rarely succeeds because of generation quality '
                                           'alone. A useful workflow separates the process into idea, visual '
                                           'generation, edit, captioning and final delivery. This makes it '
                                           'easier to choose tools based on the stage where they add value.',
                                  'sections': [{'heading': '1. Write for the first seconds',
                                                'body': 'Before generating any video, define the opening '
                                                        'visual and the first line or action. Short-form '
                                                        'viewers decide quickly whether to continue. A clear '
                                                        'visual change, surprising premise or immediate '
                                                        'problem usually gives the edit a stronger starting '
                                                        'point than a slow establishing shot.'},
                                               {'heading': '2. Generate only the shots that need AI',
                                                'body': 'Do not use generation for every second if ordinary '
                                                        'footage, graphics or text would communicate the '
                                                        'idea more clearly. Flow, Runway, Pika and Luma can '
                                                        'create unusual visual moments, while conventional '
                                                        'footage can handle context and transitions. '
                                                        'Selective generation also reduces reruns and '
                                                        'credits.'},
                                               {'heading': '3. Assemble in a real editor',
                                                'body': 'A dedicated editor such as CapCut is often the '
                                                        'practical place to control pacing, remove weak '
                                                        'frames, add captions, mix music and place sound '
                                                        'effects. The generated clip is an ingredient, not '
                                                        'necessarily the finished video.'},
                                               {'heading': '4. Check continuity on a phone screen',
                                                'body': 'Review the final export vertically and at normal '
                                                        'viewing size. Look for sudden character changes, '
                                                        'unreadable text, awkward crops and long silent '
                                                        'gaps. AI artifacts that are easy to ignore on a '
                                                        'desktop monitor may become distracting in a fast '
                                                        'vertical feed.'},
                                               {'heading': '5. Reuse a workflow, not the exact video',
                                                'body': 'Once a format works, reuse the production '
                                                        'structure: hook length, number of shots, caption '
                                                        'style and edit rhythm. Avoid duplicating the same '
                                                        'creative idea repeatedly. A repeatable process '
                                                        'saves time while still allowing every video to have '
                                                        'a new story or visual concept.'}],
                                  'takeaways': ['Plan the hook before generating shots.',
                                                'Use AI only where it adds clear visual value.',
                                                'Finish pacing, captions and audio in an editor.',
                                                'Review vertically on a phone-sized screen.',
                                                'Repeat the workflow, not the same creative idea.']},
 'background-removal-vs-product-photo-editor': {'title': 'Background Remover vs Product Photo Editor: Which '
                                                         'Tool Do You Actually Need?',
                                                'description': 'Understand when a one-click background '
                                                               'remover is enough and when a product-photo '
                                                               'workflow is the better choice.',
                                                'updated': 'September 4, 2026',
                                                'intro': 'Background removal and product-photo editing sound '
                                                         'similar, but they solve different levels of the '
                                                         'same problem. The right choice depends on whether '
                                                         'you only need a clean cutout or a repeatable '
                                                         'commercial image workflow.',
                                                'sections': [{'heading': 'Use a background remover for a '
                                                                         'single technical task',
                                                              'body': 'A focused service such as Remove.bg '
                                                                      'is efficient when the goal is simply '
                                                                      'to isolate a person or object and '
                                                                      'export a transparent result. It is '
                                                                      'useful for logos, profile images, '
                                                                      'design cutouts and occasional product '
                                                                      'photos. The main advantage is speed '
                                                                      'and a very small learning curve.'},
                                                             {'heading': 'Use a product-photo editor for '
                                                                         'repeatable commercial assets',
                                                              'body': 'PhotoRoom is better aligned with '
                                                                      'sellers who need more than '
                                                                      'transparency. Product images may need '
                                                                      'consistent backgrounds, shadows, '
                                                                      'framing and marketplace-ready '
                                                                      'presentation. When many listings need '
                                                                      'a similar look, a workflow designed '
                                                                      'around product photography can save '
                                                                      'more time.'},
                                                             {'heading': 'Complex edges still deserve '
                                                                         'inspection',
                                                              'body': 'Hair, glass, fur, translucent objects '
                                                                      'and motion blur can challenge '
                                                                      'automatic segmentation. Whichever '
                                                                      'tool you choose, zoom into the edge '
                                                                      'before publishing. A fast automatic '
                                                                      'result is useful only if the cutout '
                                                                      'remains believable against the new '
                                                                      'background.'},
                                                             {'heading': 'Match the plan to frequency',
                                                              'body': 'If you remove one background a month, '
                                                                      'a specialist commercial workflow may '
                                                                      'be unnecessary. If product images are '
                                                                      'part of daily business operations, '
                                                                      'consistency and batch efficiency can '
                                                                      'justify a more capable tool. '
                                                                      'Frequency is often a better buying '
                                                                      'signal than the raw number of '
                                                                      'features.'}],
                                                'takeaways': ['Choose a background remover for quick '
                                                              'transparent cutouts.',
                                                              'Choose a product-photo editor for repeatable '
                                                              'selling workflows.',
                                                              'Inspect difficult edges before publishing.',
                                                              'Match the plan to how often the task '
                                                              'occurs.']},
 'ai-avatar-tools-explained': {'title': 'HeyGen, D-ID and Synthesia: Understanding AI Avatar Video Tools',
                               'description': 'A practical guide to AI avatar video for marketing, training, '
                                              'explainers and presenter-led communication.',
                               'updated': 'September 4, 2026',
                               'intro': 'AI avatar platforms are often grouped with generative video, but '
                                        'their job is different. Instead of creating cinematic scenes, they '
                                        'focus on delivering a script through a digital presenter. That '
                                        'makes them most useful in communication-heavy workflows.',
                               'sections': [{'heading': 'HeyGen: presenter and marketing flexibility',
                                             'body': 'HeyGen is a natural option for marketing, product '
                                                     'explanations and repeatable presenter content. It is '
                                                     'useful when teams want scripted videos without '
                                                     'arranging a new camera shoot every time, and '
                                                     'localization can be an important part of that '
                                                     'workflow.'},
                                            {'heading': 'D-ID: talking-avatar simplicity',
                                             'body': 'D-ID is focused on turning an image, script or audio '
                                                     'input into a speaking digital person. It can be '
                                                     'effective for personalized messages, simple explainers '
                                                     'and experiments where a talking face is the central '
                                                     'element rather than a complex scene.'},
                                            {'heading': 'Synthesia: structured business communication',
                                             'body': 'Synthesia is particularly aligned with training, '
                                                     'onboarding, tutorials and business presentations. '
                                                     'Teams that need a repeatable, formal presenter format '
                                                     'may value this structure more than cinematic freedom.'},
                                            {'heading': 'When an avatar is the wrong tool',
                                             'body': 'Avatar video is not a direct replacement for actors, '
                                                     'documentary footage or cinematic generative video. If '
                                                     'emotion, natural human interaction, physical '
                                                     'demonstrations or complex environments are central to '
                                                     'the message, conventional filming or a different AI '
                                                     'video workflow may be more appropriate.'},
                                            {'heading': 'Evaluate the communication, not only the avatar',
                                             'body': 'A useful avatar video still needs a concise script, '
                                                     'clear pacing, readable on-screen information and '
                                                     'appropriate voice delivery. The technology can reduce '
                                                     'production effort, but the quality of the message '
                                                     'remains the main factor in whether the viewer '
                                                     'understands and trusts the video.'}],
                               'takeaways': ['Avatar tools are communication tools more than filmmaking '
                                             'tools.',
                                             'HeyGen fits presenter and marketing workflows.',
                                             'D-ID offers a focused talking-avatar approach.',
                                             'Synthesia is aligned with structured business and training '
                                             'content.',
                                             'Script quality still matters more than novelty.']}}
